{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837956",
      "title": "Managing & Getting User Input via State & Generic Handlers",
      "sourceHash": "79e97434599ec148f8011f3aebb67250f38305e42a8ce2e6edea2a48dee6f082",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "So therefore, here we typically want access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 6.81,
          "en": "to the values entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.81,
          "end": 11.81,
          "en": "And one way to get that access is, of course, to useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 15.873,
          "en": "So to use the useState hook, which is imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 20.13,
          "en": "And now, we could set up one piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.13,
          "end": 22.77,
          "en": "for every input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.77,
          "end": 25.38,
          "en": "or set up one combined state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.38,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "where we store all those state values in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "Both approaches would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 35.163,
          "en": "and here I'll go for the multiple state slices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 38.661,
          "en": "So we could have our enteredEmail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.661,
          "end": 42.963,
          "en": "and the setEnteredEmail state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 47.19,
          "en": "and then, also have a second piece of state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.19,
          "end": 52.148,
          "en": "in this login form where we store the enteredPassword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.148,
          "end": 55.073,
          "en": "So here we can get the enteredPassword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "and setEnteredPassword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 63.843,
          "en": "and work with these two pieces of state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 68.85,
          "en": "Now, the initial state might always be an empty string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "so that we start with no text being entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "in those input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 78.24,
          "en": "And now, we typically want to set up change listeners,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "like a new function where we handle the email change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 86.07,
          "en": "where we also get an event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 88.98,
          "en": "automatically passed in by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.98,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "And where we then set this function as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 96.87299999999999,
          "en": "to the onChange prop of this email input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 103.13,
          "en": "So handleEmailChange is now connected to this input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "and therefore, it's this function that will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "on every value change that's made on that input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 112.833,
          "en": "so every keystroke for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.75,
          "end": 118.14,
          "en": "And here we could now call setEnteredEmail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 118.14,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "and set the value to event.target.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "because the target of the event is that input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "and that underlying object that represents this input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.74,
          "en": "has a value property which gives us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 133.74,
          "end": 135.933,
          "en": "to the currently entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "Now, we just also wanna feed that value back into the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "by setting the value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 147.363,
          "en": "and by setting it equal to our state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "So that for one, we're setting our initial value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "as a value that's shown in the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "in this input field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "but also so that we feed every change the user makes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "back into this input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.09300000000002,
          "en": "so that it is reflected there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "And that is, of course, an approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 172.203,
          "en": "about which you learned way earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.07,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "With that, if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 180.53,
          "en": "I can enter values here, so that works just fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "And I can also use that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 186.3,
          "en": "in my handleSubmit function now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.3,
          "end": 191.04,
          "en": "And for example, console log user email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 195.813,
          "en": "and then output the enteredEmail here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 198.99,
          "en": "And therefore, if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 201.54,
          "en": "and I do enter some email address here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 201.54,
          "end": 205.053,
          "en": "and I click Login, I see this output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 206.57999999999998,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "So that's how we can get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 210.903,
          "en": "of that value entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 214.47,
          "en": "And therefore, now we could, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 218.447,
          "en": "also add a second function here handlePasswordChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 225.35,
          "en": "where we repeat that process for the password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.263,
          "en": "which we also set to event.target.value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "But of course, if we're creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "separate handling functions for all our inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 240.81,
          "en": "we might end up with a lot of handling functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 240.81,
          "end": 244.023,
          "en": "if we have a complex form with a lot of inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 248.043,
          "en": "And we'll end up with a lot of state snapshots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 249.18,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "Now you could work around the many state snapshots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 255.6,
          "en": "by instead using some combined state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 255.6,
          "end": 257.46,
          "en": "So an alternative here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 257.46,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "would be to have the enteredValues state, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 264.96,
          "en": "And, of course, the name as always is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 264.96,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "which might be one single object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 270.693,
          "en": "or an array of multiple values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 271.65,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "But here, I'm using an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 275.82,
          "en": "where you might have an email property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 275.82,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "and a password property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "And, of course, those property names are also up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "which initially might be set to empty strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 286.98,
          "en": "And now you could set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 286.98,
          "end": 289.563,
          "en": "one generic event handling function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 295.053,
          "en": "The handleInputChange function, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 295.95,
          "end": 299.11,
          "en": "where you call setEnteredValues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 300.12,
          "end": 304.053,
          "en": "and where you then update one of those entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 308.34,
          "en": "For that, this handleInputChange function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 308.34,
          "end": 311.19,
          "en": "must not just get the event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 311.19,
          "end": 315.33,
          "en": "but also some identifier of the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 315.33,
          "end": 317.343,
          "en": "for which the event occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 318.66,
          "end": 322.71,
          "en": "So that you could then update the entered values state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 322.71,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "by using this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "of calling this state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 331.533,
          "en": "So where you pass a function to the state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 335.67,
          "en": "so that we get the previous state snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 335.67,
          "end": 338.94,
          "en": "and we can then return a new state snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 338.94,
          "end": 341.1,
          "en": "a new object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 341.1,
          "end": 344.85,
          "en": "wrapped in parentheses here to make it clear to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 344.85,
          "end": 348.09000000000003,
          "en": "that I want to immediately return an object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 348.09000000000003,
          "end": 350.64,
          "en": "and that those curly braces here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 350.64,
          "end": 353.46,
          "en": "do not mark the function body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 353.46,
          "end": 355.83299999999997,
          "en": "but instead create an object value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 356.67,
          "end": 359.13,
          "en": "And here you would then paste in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.13,
          "end": 364.08,
          "en": "your existing key value pairs by using the spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 364.08,
          "end": 367.26,
          "en": "because I only wanna update one of these two fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 370.35,
          "en": "and of course, the other field with its current value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 370.35,
          "end": 371.733,
          "en": "should not be lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 375.21,
          "en": "And you would then update the field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 375.21,
          "end": 377.823,
          "en": "that's identified by this identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 378.75,
          "end": 381.87,
          "en": "For this, you can use a JavaScript syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381.87,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "that allows you to dynamically access a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 387.18,
          "en": "in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 387.18,
          "end": 390.66,
          "en": "by adding square brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 390.66,
          "end": 395.19,
          "en": "and then putting the variable or parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.19,
          "end": 397.44,
          "en": "that holds the name of the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 397.44,
          "end": 400.89300000000003,
          "en": "that should be set between those square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402.48,
          "end": 407.15999999999997,
          "en": "So that's how you can dynamically target and set a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 407.15999999999997,
          "end": 409.35,
          "en": "where the name of the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 409.35,
          "end": 412.263,
          "en": "is stored in a variable or parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 413.49,
          "end": 415.38,
          "en": "And then you still add a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.38,
          "end": 418.023,
          "en": "as you always do after the property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 418.95,
          "end": 420.45,
          "en": "and you set up the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 420.45,
          "end": 423.27,
          "en": "that should be stored under that property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 423.27,
          "end": 425.943,
          "en": "event.target.value, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 426.96,
          "end": 428.85,
          "en": "And that's how you could set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 428.85,
          "end": 432.963,
          "en": "a more generic, versatile change handling function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 434.46,
          "end": 437.37,
          "en": "Of course, now this function must be connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 437.37,
          "end": 439.71,
          "en": "to the input values though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 439.71,
          "end": 442.41,
          "en": "And therefore, you can't just set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 442.41,
          "end": 445.2,
          "en": "as a value for onChange anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 445.2,
          "end": 448.56,
          "en": "because React when calling this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 448.56,
          "end": 453.56,
          "en": "will not give you this identifier which we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 453.72,
          "end": 456.633,
          "en": "So that would not be provided by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 457.53,
          "end": 460.2,
          "en": "Therefore, we need more control over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 460.2,
          "end": 462.87,
          "en": "how handleInputChange will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 462.87,
          "end": 466.35,
          "en": "which we can get as you learned in this course before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 466.35,
          "end": 469.503,
          "en": "by wrapping this in an anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
